  "id": "central-auditory-abilities",
  "term": "central auditory abilities",
  "definition": "Central auditory abilities are the brain-based parts of hearing that help process sound beyond basic hearing sensitivity. In this packet, they especially include handling timing information in sound and support understanding speech, particularly when speech is distorted or heard with background noise.",
